<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Every string a player reads, in one place (DE.1). The Kotlin sources keep only developer
     text and the machine keys the gates measure by. values-de/ carries the German; the app-strings
     prose gate (harness/prose-app.js) holds both files to the style rules and refuses a key that
     exists in one language and not the other.

     What is deliberately NOT here: the core's own words. Species names, locus labels, narration
     and level text are produced by the certified Rust core and checked by gates — the German for
     those is a display overlay (res/values/narration.xml, assets/levels.de.json), never an edit
     to the core. -->
